Fix: Floating bookmark edge docking layout

- Dragging the floating bookmark header/handle can attach bookmarks to the top or bottom of the windowed overlay as a compact horizontal bookmark bar.
- The preview shows translucent placeholders for both the bookmark bar and the overlay's destination geometry; the live overlay is hidden during the drag so the preview remains clear.
- Top attachment offsets the overlay downward by the bar height; bottom attachment offsets it upward, keeping the two surfaces adjacent instead of overlapping.
- Top/bottom docking reserves screen space even while moving or resizing the floating overlay; the panel height is constrained so a bottom bar never extends past the viewport.
- Left/right attachment remains available and does not reserve vertical space.
- Edge detection measures distance to the actual panel-edge segments and prefers top/bottom at corner ties, so dragging the drawer header vertically can reach horizontal docking more naturally.
- Added a grip to the horizontal bar so it can be dragged back to a side.
- Hiding bookmarks or changing the attachment edge reverses/recalculates the reserved offset without accumulating movement.
- Updated README usage notes.
- Included a full copy of all 18 current root extension files; only content.js, defaults.js, README.md, tp-bookmarks.js, and tp-css.js differ. Backup and previous Changes folders are excluded.
